VERDICT: ✅ F1 does not fire — the axis is WIRED and the pooled magnitude is in band.
         ⚠️  BUT a per-target prediction (P-2) MISSED. F1 is the only VOID condition,
             so the arm is still cleared — but the miss is a prediction error of MINE,
             not a fault in the intervention, and it must be read before the arm runs.
             CAUSE: the prereg projected `body_A = body_positives * (P/N)` using the
             median positive FRACTION. That identity holds per step, NOT after
             averaging over steps: `positives` divides by a per-step count that is
             often 0 or 1, so mean(S/P) is dominated by the small-P steps while
             mean(S/N) is not, so one multiplicative factor cannot carry the window
             mean across. It is the mean-of-ratios vs ratio-of-means error, on the
             target where P is smallest — exactly where the two diverge most.
             DIRECTION: the miss is UPWARD. ns lands at 0.175 of its gate, not 0.058,
             so the per-target spread under A is ~1.7x (0.297/0.175/0.204), not the 5x
             the prereg's skepticism ledger warned about. A is MORE even-handed
             than my own projection claimed — weakening prereg section 3.1 further.
